[
  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "name_prefix" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [
            "Heredoc",
            [
              "EOF",
              "\nA prefix that will be added to all created resources.\nThere is no default delimiter applied between the prefix and the resource name.\nPlease include the delimiter in the actual prefix.\n\nExample:\n```\nname_prefix = \"test-\"\n```\n\n**Note!** \\\nThis prefix is not applied to existing resources. If you plan to reuse i.e. a VNET please specify it's full name,\neven if it is also prefixed with the same value as the one in this property.\n"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "default", [ "String", "" ] ],
        [ "Attribute", "type", [ "Id", "string" ] ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "create_resource_group" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [
            "Heredoc",
            [
              "EOF",
              "\nWhen set to `true` it will cause a Resource Group creation.\nName of the newly specified RG is controlled by `resource_group_name`.\n\nWhen set to `false` the `resource_group_name` parameter is used to specify a name of an existing Resource Group.\n"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "default", [ "Bool", true ] ],
        [ "Attribute", "type", [ "Id", "bool" ] ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "resource_group_name" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [ "String", "Name of the Resource Group." ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "type", [ "Id", "string" ] ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "region" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [ "String", "The Azure region to use." ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "type", [ "Id", "string" ] ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "tags" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [ "String", "Map of tags to assign to the created resources." ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "default", [ "Object", [] ] ],
        [
          "Attribute",
          "type",
          [ "Fun_call", [ "map", [ [ "Id", "string" ] ] ] ]
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "vnets" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [
            "Heredoc",
            [
              "EOF",
              "\nA map defining VNETs.\n\nFor detailed documentation on each property refer to [module documentation](../../modules/vnet/README.md)\n\n- `create_virtual_network`                   - (`bool`, optional, defaults to `true`) when set to `true` will create a VNET,\n                                               `false` will source an existing VNET.\n- `name`                                     - (`string`, required) a name of a VNET. In case `create_virtual_network = false`\n                                               this should be a full resource name, including prefixes.\n- `resource_group_name`                      - (`string`, optional, defaults to current RG) a name of an existing Resource\n                                               Group in which the VNET will reside or is sourced from.\n- `address_space`                            - (`list`, required when `create_virtual_network = false`) a list of CIDRs for a\n                                               newly created VNET.\n- `dns_servers`                              - (`list`, optional, defaults to module defaults) a list of IP addresses of custom\n                                               DNS servers (by default Azure DNS is used).\n- `vnet_encryption`                          - (`string`, optional, defaults to module default) enables Azure Virtual Network\n                                               Encryption when set, only possible value at the moment is `AllowUnencrypted`. \n                                               When set to `null`, the feature is disabled.\n- `ddos_protection_plan_name`                - (`string`, optional, defaults to `null`) name of an existing Azure Network DDOS\n                                               Protection Plan to be associated with the VNET.\n- `ddos_protection_plan_resource_group_name` - (`string`, optional, defaults to `null`) name of the Resource Group containing\n                                               an existing Azure Network DDOS Protection Plan to be associated with the VNET.\n- `network_security_groups`                  - (`map`, optional) map of Network Security Groups to create, for details see\n                                               [VNET module documentation](../../modules/vnet/README.md#network_security_groups).\n- `route_tables`                             - (`map`, optional) map of Route Tables to create, for details see\n                                               [VNET module documentation](../../modules/vnet/README.md#route_tables).\n- `subnets`                                  - (`map`, optional) map of Subnets to create or source, for details see\n                                               [VNET module documentation](../../modules/vnet/README.md#subnets).\n"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "Attribute",
          "type",
          [
            "Fun_call",
            [
              "map",
              [
                [
                  "Fun_call",
                  [
                    "object",
