  [
    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "natgws" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [
            "Heredoc",
            [
              "EOF",
              "\nA map defining NAT Gateways.\n\nPlease note that a NAT Gateway is a zonal resource, this means it's always placed in a zone (even when you do not specify one\nexplicitly). Please refer to Microsoft documentation for notes on NAT Gateway's zonal resiliency.\nFor detailed documentation on each property refer to [module documentation](../../modules/natgw/README.md).\n\nFollowing properties are supported:\n- `name`                - (`string`, required) a name of a NAT Gateway. In case `create_natgw = false` this should be a full\n                          resource name, including prefixes.\n- `vnet_key`            - (`string`, required) a name (key value) of a VNET defined in `var.vnets` that hosts a subnet this\n                          NAT Gateway will be assigned to.\n- `subnet_keys`         - (`list(string)`, required) a list of subnets (key values) the NAT Gateway will be assigned to,\n                          defined in `var.vnets` for a VNET described by `vnet_name`.\n- `create_natgw`        - (`bool`, optional, defaults to `true`) create (`true`) or source an existing NAT Gateway (`false`),\n                          created or sourced: the NAT Gateway will be assigned to a subnet created by the `vnet` module.\n- `resource_group_name` - (`string`, optional) name of a Resource Group hosting the NAT Gateway (newly created or the existing\n                          one).\n- `zone`                - (`string`, optional) an Availability Zone in which the NAT Gateway will be placed, when skipped\n                          Azure will pick a zone.\n- `idle_timeout`        - (`number`, optional, defults to 4) connection IDLE timeout in minutes, for newly created resources.\n- `public_ip`           - (`object`, optional) an object defining a public IP resource attached to the NAT Gateway.\n- `public_ip_prefix`    - (`object`, optional) an object defining a public IP prefix resource attached to the NAT Gatway.\n\nExample:\n```\nnatgws = {\n  \"natgw\" = {\n    name        = \"natgw\"\n    vnet_key    = \"transit-vnet\"\n    subnet_keys = [\"management\"]\n    public_ip = {\n      create = true\n      name   = \"natgw-pip\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "default", [ "Object", [] ] ],
        [
          "Attribute",
          "type",
          [
            "Fun_call",
            [
              "map",
              [
                [
                  "Fun_call",
                  [
                    "object",
                    [
                      [
                        "Object",
                        [
                          [ [ "Bare", "name" ], [ "Id", "string" ] ],
                          [ [ "Bare", "vnet_key" ], [ "Id", "string" ] ],
                          [
                            [ "Bare", "subnet_keys" ],
                            [
                              "Fun_call", [ "list", [ [ "Id", "string" ] ] ]
                            ]
                          ],
                          [
                            [ "Bare", "create_natgw" ],
                            [
